## b7e4aaffabac

**Result: No issue found in the bounded audit.**

I checked 720 generated scenes: all 12 declared profiles, all three difficulty bands, and 20 seeds per profile/band. For every scene, the analyzer/self-check accepted it, the explicit profile override round-tripped, the Python audit rule changed exactly the declared bridge cells, and both horizontal and vertical orientations appeared. I also checked all eight canonical input/output pairs across the two canonical occurrences; each was accepted, mapped to one of the four public profiles, and matched the audit rule.

Measured coverage from `checks/audits/audit_probe.json`:

- 720 generated scenes;
- exactly 60 observations of each declared profile;
- 342 horizontal and 378 vertical scenes;
- eight canonical pairs matched.

I specifically looked for one-axis-only generation, profile aliases, full-overlap instead of shrunken-overlap painting, edge failures, and public-profile drift. None reproduced. This is not a proof against every semantic shortcut; it is a clean result for those concrete checks.

The target's packaged pytest file could not be collected directly from source because it imports the staged `puzzle_generators.per_puzzle` namespace. That is a tooling/layout issue recorded in `FEEDBACK_TO_CODEX.md`, not a generator defect. The standalone probe imports the selected source file directly and preserves its results.
